# core/data/talk/grammar/en/follow.tlk - keep the talk going (owner: TK; talk_dm.c DK_FOLLOW,
# TGE_FOLLOW; docs/TALK.md "Keeping the talk going").
#
# After a resident answers the player, and when the talk opens, the same resident hands the talk
# back: a question about the topic, a remark that goes with it, or a way out of a spat. Which rule
# fits comes from what the player just did: a change of subject (act=change_topic), a kind line
# (pact=warm), a snarky one (pact=cool: push on or let it go, so the player can heat the room up
# or cool it down), or plain talk. Said to the player. Kid-safe everywhere: no register word here.

# ---- the subject changed ---------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule follow.switch guard: topic&act=change_topic act: ask_about
  "Oh, {x}? Okay. What got you onto {x}?"
  "Sudden {x}. I respect it. What's the story, {you}?"
  "Sure, let's do {x}. You go first."
  "Hm, {x}. Fine by me. Where do you want to start?"
@rule follow.switch.fear guard: fears_topic&act=change_topic act: tell
  "{x:cap}? Can we go slow on that one? It gives me the shivers."
  "Okay, {x}. But I'm sitting closer to the door."
@rule follow.switch.love guard: likes_topic&act=change_topic act: ask_about
  "{x:cap}! Finally. Ask me anything."
  "Now you're talking. I have so many thoughts on {x}."

# ---- the player was kind ----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule follow.warm guard: topic&pact=warm&!act=change_topic act: ask_about
  "That's kind of you. Now, what do you think of {x}?"
  "Aw. Okay, now I'm in a good mood. Tell me more about {x}."
@rule follow.warm.open guard: !topic&pact=warm&!act=change_topic act: ask_feeling
  "That helps, {you}. How are you doing, really?"
  "You're nice to talk to. What's been going on with you?"

# ---- the player was snarky: push on, or let it go ----------------------------------------------------
@rule follow.cool guard: pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_feeling
  "Is that how we're doing this? Because I can do that too."
  "Okay, ouch. Do we keep going, or take a breath?"
  "You want to push on this, or shake on it?"
  "Careful, {you}. I'm only a little bit fragile."
@rule follow.cool.blunt guard: blunt&pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_feeling
  "Say that again and see what happens. Or don't. Your pick."
@rule follow.cool.polite guard: polite&pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_feeling
  "I'd like us to stay friends. Can we do that, {you}?"

# ---- plain talk: hand it back --------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule follow.ask guard: topic&!pact=cool&!pact=warm&!act=change_topic act: ask_opinion
  "What's your take on {x}, {you}?"
  "Anything about {x} bug you? Or delight you?"
  "Have you ever tried {x}? Be honest."
  "Does {x} come up a lot for you?"
@rule follow.ask.love guard: likes_topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_opinion
  "I could talk about {x} all day. What's your angle?"
  "{x:cap} is my favourite. Is it yours?"
@rule follow.ask.fear guard: fears_topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: tell
  "Can we talk about something else after this? {x:cap} makes my ears ring."
@rule follow.open guard: !topic&!pact=cool&!pact=warm&!act=change_topic act: ask_about
  "So what else is going on with you?"
  "Anything else on your mind, {you}?"
  "Keep going. I'm listening. Mostly."
  "Pick anything. I'll pretend I picked it too."
@rule follow.blunt guard: blunt&topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_opinion
  "Opinion on {x}. Go."
  "{x:cap}. Yes or no?"
@rule follow.polite guard: polite&topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_opinion
  "If it's not too much to ask, what do you make of {x}?"
  "I'd love to hear what you think about {x}."
@rule follow.quirky guard: quirky&topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: ask_opinion
  "Quick: {x}. First word that pops out."
  "Tell me one weird fact about {x}. Weird is better."
@rule follow.kid guard: kid_speaker&topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic tags: kid act: ask_opinion
  "Do you like {x}? I like {x}! Do you?"
  "Can we talk about {x} more? Please?"
@rule follow.elder guard: elder&topic&!pact=cool&!act=change_topic act: tell
  "{x:cap}. Now there's a word I haven't heard in a while. Go on."
